                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "During National Nurses Week, we recognize the hardworking and caring nurses of #IL01. Thank you for your dedication to your patients and commitment to providing lifesaving care at every stage of life. \n\nAs we honor those who have dedicated their lives to ensuring the well-being of others, we celebrate leaders like Mary Eliza Mahoney, the first Black professionally trained nurse in the United States. A symbol of resilience and excellence, Mahoney broke racial barriers in healthcare, paving the way for future generations of nurses through her advocacy for equity, professionalism, and compassionate care.",
